+### Matched-size Secure BP: single run (seed 42)
+
+One execution of `bp_matched_matrix.mpc` completed with exit status 0: the
+`784-128-128-10` network, 5,000/1,000/1,000 MNIST examples (a subset, not the
+full 60,000-image training set), five epochs, batch size 128, SGD at 0.05,
+seed 42, MP-SPDZ v0.4.4, Rep3 Ring, 64-bit ring, `sfix(16,31)`, three parties
+on one machine (localhost). The recorded result is 772/1,000 test examples
+correct (77.2%), equal to the plaintext seed-42 reference recorded in
+`results/baselines/bp.csv`. The report records 933.263 seconds of MP-SPDZ time
+and 5,224.49 MB of global communication.
+
+This is a single-seed feasibility result. It is not a multi-seed benchmark,
+not a performance comparison, not production-scale training and not a security
+proof. Known limitations:
+
+- One seed; no variance estimate and no repeated runs.
+- Localhost execution says nothing about network performance; MP-SPDZ time and
+  external wall-clock time cover different scopes, and the hardware used is not
+  recorded in the run artifacts.
+- The protocol assumes three semi-honest parties with an honest majority. It
+  does not provide malicious security, and no formal security proof is claimed.
+- Fixed-point arithmetic and probabilistic truncation can make secure results
+  differ numerically from plaintext training.
+- The plaintext reference values come from the recorded seed-42 baseline and
+  were not re-run for this comparison. The checkpoint policy also differs
+  (plaintext: validation-selected; secure: epoch 5). The equal test accuracy is
+  a descriptive match for one seed, not evidence that secure training is
+  equivalent to or better than plaintext training.
+- The run log reports that the computation domain is too small for low-round
+  truncation (at least 103 bits needed). Its numerical and security impact is
+  unresolved.
+- The raw run log, input bundle and Player-Data backup are kept outside this
+  repository; the evidence here is the written report, `results.csv` and the
+  integrity manifest in
+  [`docs/experimental-results/secure-bp-full-run/`](docs/experimental-results/secure-bp-full-run/).
+  Earlier full-size attempts under `results/mpc/bp/` did not complete and must
+  not be combined with this result.
+
